    "updated_at": "2016-11-28T12:13:49Z",
    "body": "The change is:\r\n\r\n* Remove the scoping to `article` element.\r\n* Allow physical address or digital location or contact information for anything.\r\n\r\nThe reasoning is something like:\r\n\r\n* People use it for contact information for site owner, contact information for article, copyright information, and physical addresses (may or may not be contact information for the site/article).\r\n* No known software exists that uses the semantic of `address`.\r\n* No software is expected to exist to use the broader semantic of `address`, either, but may exist for schema.org-annotated things.\r\n\r\nDid I understand correctly?",
